{"nodes": [{"id": "readme_house_control", "label": "House Control", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "A home as a live 3D model in the Mac menu bar, around the notch and on the iPhone, controlling lights and air conditioners through Smart Life, Home Assistant, Philips Hue and Apple Home. A small native Swift shell around one Three.js web UI, with no frameworks, no Electron, no server and no account of its own."}, {"id": "readme_three_js_web_ui", "label": "Single Three.js Web UI Shared by Both Apps", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Both apps are a small native Swift shell (AppKit on the Mac, SwiftUI on the iPhone) around one Three.js web UI, sharing device clients and sync as a Swift package, so the 3D scene, panel, island, editor and AI Access window are written once while each platform keeps native chrome."}, {"id": "readme_native_swift_shell", "label": "Native Swift Shell (AppKit / SwiftUI)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_menu_bar_panel", "label": "Menu Bar Panel", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Click the house icon and a panel drops down; click anywhere else and it is gone. There is no Dock icon and no main window, so the app lives where a quick control belongs."}, {"id": "readme_island", "label": "The Island Around the Notch", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "A black tab grows out of the MacBook notch and springs open on hover with the 3D model, scenes and devices. It peeks out to report changes but never takes the keyboard from the app in use."}, {"id": "readme_floor_plan_json", "label": "Floor Plan as One JSON File (plan.json)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Rooms, walls, doors, windows and furniture are built from a single JSON document, so swapping the file swaps the home, and it can be written by hand, versioned, exported or imported."}, {"id": "readme_editor", "label": "Visual Home Editor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_device_platforms", "label": "Four Device Platforms Mixed in One Home", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_simulated_devices", "label": "Simulated Devices Until Sign-In", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Until a platform is connected every device is simulated, so the app and its demo plans can be tried end to end before any hardware or account exists."}, {"id": "readme_scenes", "label": "Scenes", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_ai_access", "label": "AI Access", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Give ChatGPT, Claude or any assistant a private link or MCP address served by the Mac itself; Stop or the auto-stop timer makes the address disappear, and device IDs and sign-ins never leave the Mac."}, {"id": "readme_widgets", "label": "Widgets and Controls", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_iphone_app", "label": "iPhone App That Needs No Mac", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "The whole home can be set up on the phone, so pairing a Mac is optional; a paired Mac only adds two-way sync."}, {"id": "readme_iphone_editions", "label": "App Store and Smart Life iPhone Editions", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Smart Life is reached through the sign-in Home Assistant's Tuya integration uses, not an API Tuya offers to apps, so it stays out of the App Store edition entirely; the editions are separate apps (bundle id and App Group) and can sit on one phone."}, {"id": "readme_sync_mac_iphone", "label": "Mac-to-iPhone Sync over Bonjour and TLS", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "The Mac advertises itself with Bonjour and the two talk over TLS with a pre-shared key that only the QR code carries, so nothing goes through a server and a device that never saw the code cannot connect."}, {"id": "readme_ad_hoc_signing", "label": "Ad-Hoc Signing Instead of Notarization", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Notarizing needs an Apple Developer ID, and that certificate carries a person's legal name inside every copy of the app. House Control ships signed ad hoc instead and earns trust the open-source way: all code public, releases built in public, and users can build it themselves."}, {"id": "readme_build_provenance_attestation", "label": "Build Provenance Attestation", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "Every release image is built by GitHub Actions from the tagged commit and carries a SHA-256 plus a signed provenance attestation, so users can verify origin without a paid signing certificate."}, {"id": "readme_privacy_no_backend", "label": "No Backend and No Telemetry", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "The app talks only to the platforms the user connects, with no telemetry and no backend of its own; the single exception is AI Access's Cloudflare tunnel, which the user switches on and off."}, {"id": "readme_environment_variables", "label": "HOUSE_* Environment Variables", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_selftests_diagnose", "label": "Offline Self-Checks and --diagnose", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_release_process", "label": "Mac Release Process: Tag to Draft Release", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_limitations", "label": "Known Limitations", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}, {"id": "readme_support_crypto", "label": "Crypto Tips as Project Support", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md", "rationale": "The app is free with no ads; tips in crypto fund more devices, platforms and fixes, and a star, bug report or pull request is stated to help just as much."}, {"id": "readme_licence_mit", "label": "MIT Licence", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "README.md"}], "edges": [{"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_three_js_web_ui", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_menu_bar_panel", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_island", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_floor_plan_json", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_editor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_device_platforms", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_ai_access", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_widgets", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_iphone_app", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.md", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "readme_house_control", "target": "readme_privacy_no_backend", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "README.